      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 457603573,
          "type": null,
          "body": "This patch looks good on macOS but fails to compile on Ubuntu due to version of Qt (Currently my Ubuntu dev VM has Qt 5.9.5).  QFontMetrics::horizontalAdvance() was introduced in in Qt 5.11.\n\nShould the use of horizontalAdvance() versus boundingRect().width() be protected with the following?\n\n```\n   #if (QT_VERSION >= QT_VERSION_CHECK(5, 11, 0))\n       ... horizontalAdvance ...\n   #else\n       ... boundingRect(line).width() ...\n   #endf\n```\n\nObviously this won't resolve #17033 for pre Qt 5.11 users.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6682068,
            "username": "jim.young",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Jim Young",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
